<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00176</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dfbe91a7-480b-452b-ae56-85c1c0d66eb0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">For questions 1 – 3, choose an equivalent equation.</para>
      <exercise id="b52a52a3-95d8-4b74-8c07-2cb024e1c0f1" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Which equation is equivalent to \(3x + 6 = 4x + 7\)?</para>
          <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">\(7x=1\)</para>
          <para id="para-00006">\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00007">\(9x=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00008">\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00009">\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00010">Correct! \(3x-1=4x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00011">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00012">The correct answer is \(3x-1=4x\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_942bfea6-ff71-4594-9ff9-fe0e6d190ec5" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00013">Which equation is equivalent to \(3(x + 6) = 4x + 7\)?</para>
          <para id="para-00014">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00015">\(7x=1\)</para>
          <para id="para-00016">\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00017">\(9x=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00018">\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00019">\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00020">Correct! \(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">The correct answer is \(3x+18=4x+7\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="fd402ad6-ad05-4fe4-ac10-b4a4ad5a6585" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00023">Which equation is equivalent to \(4x + 3x = 7-6\)?</para>
          <para id="para-00024">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00025">\(7x=1\)</para>
          <para id="para-00026">\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00027">\(9x=4x+7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00028">\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00029">\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00030">Correct! \(7x=1\)</para>
          <para id="para-00031">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00032">The correct answer is \(7x=1\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_64df16ad-469d-4280-8bcc-52d29d144939" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00033">Select three equations that have 0 as a solution.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00034">Correct! \(2x+10=4x+10\), \(4x=9x\), and \(2x-3+4x=4-7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00035">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.1.</para>
          <para id="para-00036">The correct answers are \(2x+10=4x+10\), \(4x=9x\), and \(2x-3+4x=4-7\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a05374c2-76ac-4ff2-99f4-8ddb1069cabc" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00037">Which equation is equivalent to \(6(x-3)=24\)?</para>
          <para id="para-00038">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00039">\(6x-3=24\)</para>
          <para id="para-00040">\(x-3=4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00041">\(6x=21\)</para>
          <para id="para-00042">\(6x=27\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00043">Correct! \(x-3=4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00044">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00045">The correct answer is \(x-3=4\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5764b7ed-1940-478d-8431-e5ca9c6ba19a" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00046">Which of the following sets of equations are equivalent to each other?</para>
          <para id="para-00047">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00048">\(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\)</para>
          <para id="para-00049">\(7(x+2)=21\) and \(7x +2=21\)</para>
          <para id="para-00050">\(5x - 2 = 7x +4\) and \(12x -2 =4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00051">\(6x-4=11\) and \(6x =7\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00052">Correct! \(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\). Each side of the equation was divided by 5. So the equations are equivalent.</para>
          <para id="para-00053">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00054">The correct answer is \(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\). Each side of the equation was divided by 5. So the equations are equivalent.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_2fdde9ea-4d45-43f3-9578-2d046e7b548d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00055">Using the distributive property, choose which equation would be an equivalent equation to \(3(x-2) =7\).</para>
          <para id="para-00056">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00057">\(3x-2=7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00058">\(3x-6=7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00059">\(x-2=4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00060">\(3x=9\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00061">Correct! \(3x - 6 =7\)</para>
          <para id="para-00062">Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00063">The correct answer is \(3x - 6 =7\). It is one of the solutions that could be equivalent to \(3(x-2) =7\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
